<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.9 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.9 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.9 percent in the week to Feb 26 over the equivalent year-ago week, data released by the Bank of England showed. Last week the annual rise was 6.2 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week  pvs week	yr-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     20.07	 20.58	   19.45</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	   2.02	  1.93	    1.83</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
